# Which kits take the commits on this branch.
#
# One device id per line; shell globs allowed; `#` comments and blank lines
# ignored. Read by scripts/self_update.sh from the commit being offered, so
# the push itself decides who takes it.
#
#   *          the whole fleet -- the normal state
#   P002       only the bench kit, to prove a change before it reaches a car
#   P00[12]    a named subset
#
# Leave this at `*` unless a rollout is actually in progress, and put it back
# in the same session: a kit left off the list silently stops updating, and
# nothing on the kit says why except one line in `journalctl -u obd-ev-update`.
#
# A missing or empty file means every kit, so deleting it is also a safe way
# back. `sudo ./scripts/self_update.sh --force` on a kit ignores this
# entirely.
*
